  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REDUCING HUMAN-ELEPHANT CONFLICT IN THE IMENTI FOREST RESERVE AND RESTORING HABITAT CONNECTIVITY FOR THE WIDER ELEPHANT RANGE - PHASE 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT AN ELEPHANT CONSERVATION EFFORT IN THE IMENTI FOREST RESERVE BY STRENGTHENING ELEPHANT PROTECTION AND COMMUNITY ENGAGEMENT. LOCATED WITHIN THE LAIKIPIA-SAMBURU ECOSYSTEM SAVANNA ELEPHANT STRONGHOLD, THE IMENTI RESERVE IS PART OF THE MOUNT KENYA PROTECTED AREA COMPLEX, WHICH IS HOME TO APPROXIMATELY 2,500 ELEPHANTS. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE AFRICAN SAVANNA ELEPHANTS AND THEIR HABITAT BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF HUMAN-ELEPHANT CONFLICT (HEC) AND POACHING. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) DEPLOYING ANTI-POACHING PATROLS AND INSTALLING A RANGER OBSERVATION STATION AND (2) CONDUCTING A COMMUNITY SURVEY TO DETERMINE THE MOST APPROPRIATE LOCATION FOR ELEPHANT-PROOF SHORT FENCING AND CONSTRUCTION OF THE SHORT FENCING.</narrative>
  </description>
